# Line endings.
#
# .editorconfig already asks editors for `end_of_line = lf`, but nothing there
# is enforced by git: a contributor whose editor ignores it, or who has
# core.autocrlf=true (the default on Windows installs, and on GitHub's Windows
# runners), can still introduce CRLF. This makes LF true in the repository and
# in every working tree regardless of platform or local git config.
#
# The index was already 100% LF when this file was added — 81 text files, zero
# CRLF — so it normalises nothing and introduces no churn. It is preventive.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.vsix binary
